course: dictionary
lesson: 7389
title: Plunge: a sudden fall or dive
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Plunge means to jump or fall suddenly and steeply, especially into water. «Kingfishers plunge in beak first» tells you the bird drops very fast, head first. Look for clue words like down, into and in: they show where the plunge goes.
explain: The same word can describe numbers and temperatures. In the news you might read «temperatures plunged» overnight. Ask what would fit: the temperature did not climb, it dropped fast and by a lot, so plunge means fall suddenly.
explain: Plunge can also mean to push something in quickly and hard, as in «an ostrich plunges its head into the sand». Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if «dives into» still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: Plunge means to jump or fall suddenly and steeply, especially into water.
fact: «Plunge» can also mean a sudden fall in prices or temperatures: it drops fast, and by a lot.
fact: «Plunged into darkness» means all the light suddenly goes out.
fact: «Take the plunge» means finally do something brave or new.
fact: A plunge is also a noun: it is a sudden jump, a fall, or a quick swim.
exercise: «A great grey owl can plunge through deep snow to grab a vole.» What does plunge mean here? | To sing loudly | *To dive down suddenly and quickly | To melt away slowly | To walk slowly over
exercise: Ella says, «Temperatures plunged last night.» What does she mean? | They stayed exactly the same | They rose slowly | They were measured in metres | *They fell suddenly by a lot
exercise: «Dad said, let's take the plunge and buy the bike.» What does take the plunge mean? | Jump off a cliff | *Finally do something brave or new | Count to ten | Go for a swim
test: «The room was plunged into darkness when the power went out.» What does plunged into darkness mean? | To be lit by a bright lamp | To be painted black slowly | To be cleaned very carefully | *To lose all light suddenly
test: Which word means nearly the same as plunge when prices fall fast? | Sing | Wait | *Drop | Rise
exam: «She plunged into her painting with great energy.» What does plunged into mean? | Spilled the paint | *Started eagerly and with energy | Stopped painting for a rest | Fell off her chair
